      "message": "Let\u0027s do something a little bit less \"normal\". The point of sanitization is to prevent unusual and dangerous stuff, so to maximize test utility it\u0027s important to *not* build a very tame and well-behaved object.\n\nSuggestions of things to change :\n\n- setOwnerUid to something that\u0027s not my process, but something completely different\n- setAdministratorUids to a list of multiple UIDs that don\u0027t even include the owner UID\n- setNetworkSpecifier to something specific and unusual, e.g. EthernetNetworkSpecifier with an interface name of \"foobar\"\n- setTransportInfo to some WiFiInfo with unusual parameters\n- setRequestorUid to some random integer\n- setUids to some range that overlaps multiple users\n- setAllowedUids to a list of a few integers not even including the ownerUid\n\nThe rest is fine. Note that subscription IDS are currently using the ownerUid which is completely unrelated (and therefore fine in this case :) ), but maybe it\u0027s a bit easier to understand if you just pass 4 and 7 or something.\n\nAlso do add a comment that this builds an usual object to maximize the chance that this requires sanitization, so we have a high chance to detect any changes to the original.",
